        <p>PRIVATE T. ADAMS. Wounded:</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-10-28_WidnesExaminer_art0092" n="art0092">
        <head>LANCE-CORPL. T. BEN lON.</head>
        <p>LANCE-CORPL. T. BEN lON.</p>
        <p>One Of The Dardanelles' Heroes Officially Reported Killed.</p>
        <p>Responding to his country's call almost at the commencement of hostilities, Lance- Corporal Tom Benion; South Lancashire Regi- ment, was drafted to the Dardanelles in July, 1915, and after taking part in many gallant explofts was reported "missing" on August 9th, 1915. Hopes were entertained by Ulf members of his family and friends in War- rington that he might be a prisoner-of-war in the. .hands of ,the Turks; but on Tuesday of this week Mrs. T. Benion, the wife of tile brave Lance-Corporal, received official news from the War Office to the effect that her husband was killed on August 9th, 1915— fifteen months ago—during an engagement in the Dardanelles.. Mrs. Benion and her only child now reside at 13, Thelwall-lane, and Much sympathy is extended to them in their</p>
        <p>great loss. ; Lance-Corporal T. Benion, who was 27 years of age, was in the employ of the Firth: Co. before enlisting. He was an `` old boys)! of. Wycliffe ,Day School, and also worshipped :at the Wycliffe Congregational Church. La'nee-Co7-”or,vl *Benion has .several relative§ serving with the -colours, and only last week one of his cousins—Private Sam Benion—was</p>
