      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-10-28_WidnesExaminer_art0102" n="art0102">
        <head>PRIVATE FRED BRANDWOOD:</head>
        <p>PRIVATE FRED BRANDWOOD:</p>
        <p>In A London Hospital With Kidno Trouble.</p>
        <p>Nine l'eel-ts' service in the trenches by Privata Fred Brandwodi. of • Lilford-street, have been suspended owing to his being cOnve3'ed to 1. London hospital suffering from serious kidney trouble. His parents, Mr.. and Mrs.4,:randwood, have been to pay him a visit, and are gratified with. the skilful attention he is receiving. They went last Saturday, and it is an interesting co- incidence that their visit to him in hospital was exactly twelve months to the day following his enlistment in the South Lancs. Regiment. Private Brandwood, who is nineteen years of age, went to work for Messrs. Edwin Richard- son and Sons, grocers, on leaving Wycliffe- School. • He is a member of Wycliffe P.S.A., where sympathetic references were made regard- ing him at their meeting on Sunday. He k also a member of the Wycliffe Cricket Club, and has attended the evening classes at the Secandary School. His father, Mr. John Brandwood, is a popular personality, and has been employed on the L. and N.-W: Railway for over fifty years.</p>
      </div>
