        <p>' mliE CORPORATION OF WARRINGTON I. is prepared to receive LOANS either for six months' notice, or for a term of years. Applications, stating amount for investment, to be made to the Borough Treasurer, Municipal Offices, Warrington. RICHMOND'S WAR 'EMPLOYES. ADDRESSES WANTED. The Richmond's Employes' War Fund Relief , Committee intend to send Christmas Parcels to their 465 fellow-workmen who have joined the Colours. Wiil relatives or friends send the name, rank, regimental number, and battalion of these employes, in order that their parcels may be ad- dressed correctly? JOHN FAIRCLOUGH, Richmond's Works, Gracnenhall. W.rrinm+n,</p>
        <p>WIIITECROSS WORKS EMPLOYES' WAR FUND. With the object of distributing a second lot of Parcels, the Committee appeal to the Relatives and Friends to send in names and addresses of those who have enlisted or been called up from the employ of THE WHITECROSS CO.. LTD. State the Regimental number, Regiment, Sm., also notify any change of address that may take place between now and December 16th. 1916. Send particulars to The Whitecross Social and Recreation Club, Green- street, Warrington • or to I#.,F. WARING, Chairman of Committee, Whitecross Works. CROSFIELD'S WORKS COUNCIL. THE MEMBERS of the above Council are particularly desirous of assisting their fellow employes who are taking part in active War Ser- vice. and they suggest the forwarding of -A PARCEL TO EACH ONE. The whole of the expense will be defrayed -by the Employes' War Fund Account. Will the friends of Crosfield's men on Active Ser- vice kindly forward their names, battalion, and regimental- number to ,the undersigned. The last day for sending in names. Sm., is Wednesday next, November Ist, after which no further particulars can be dealt with. Mr. W. E. CLEGG, Chairman of the Works Council, Messrs. Jos. Crosfield 8; Sons, Ltd., Bank Quay, Warrington.</p>
