        <p>INFLUENZA COLDS . And Children's Coughs Cured By . Veno's Lightning Cough Cure. Mrs. Slade, 80, Lancefield-street, Queen's Park, Paddington, London, wig :—"Veno's Lightning Cough Cure has been a real blessing in my family. It cured my little boy of whooping cough when other things proved useless, and since then I have taken it myself for influenza, for which I find it splendid. It also cured baby's bronchitis. There is nothing like Veno's." Trust Veno's to cure Coughs, Colds, Asthma, Bronchitis, Influenza, Catarrh, and Whooping Cough. Prices Ild., 1/3, and 3/-, everywhere. NORTH WALES STEAMERS. Ten .Per ,Cent. For Shareholders Of The Company. The directors of the Liverpool and North Wales Steamship Co., Ltd., in their 26th annual +report, state that in addition to La Marguerite, St. Seiriol, and St. Ehies, the Admiralty requisitioned the Snowdon in November, 1915, and the withdrawal Of these four steamers necessitated a material alteration in the conduct of the company's business': The sailings on the North Wales station have,- however, been main- tained with regularity by the St. eTrillo.* This branch of the company's service was well patronised, notwithstanding the disorganisation of the usual holiday arrangements. After de- ducting the sum of £lO,OOO for depreciation on steamers, investments, &amp;c., the amount avail- able for dividend and other purposes, including the balance brought forward from last year,. is £8,703 19s. Bd., out of which the directors reoom, mend a payment of 10 per cent. dividend (less income tax), carrying forward a balance of £2,333 19s. Bd. The director retiring by rotation is Sir R. Williams Bulkeley, Bart., who is eligible for re-election.</p>
