        <p>STRANGERS AND FOREIGNERS. Warning To Lodging-House Keepers As To Need For Registration. It will be well for people who take in lodgeis to remember that the country is at war, and that under the Regulations of the Aliens Re- striction (Consolidation) Order, 1916, it is. necessary for everyone who takes in a lodger to isk him to sign a register and to see that he does it. Failure to do this renders the person taking in the lodger liable to heavy penalties. • Another point about taking in lodgers is that should they happen to hoof any other nation-. ality than British the police must be informed of the fact. Many people do not appear to know this until it is too late and they receive a summons calling them before the magis- trates. Very early on in the year one landlady was fined very heavily for failing to require a man to register. It was afterwards found that the man was an alien and had boasted of having fought in the Franco-Prussian War. The enemy spy in our midst does, really exist even at the present time, and it behoveet lodging-house keepers and others taking in lodgers to obey the law. Our worthy Chief Constable is determined to prosecute with the utmost rigour of the law anyone caught offend- ing in this respect.</p>
