        <p>reported in these columns as having been killed whilst serving his King and country. PRIVATE W. ROSE. ?toyed A Fearless Part In The Recent Successes. Private Win.. Rose, _South Lanes. Regiment, whose wife lives at 1, Clegg-street, has been itilled in action, as reported in last Saturday's "Examiner." By an error the, wr.)ng portrait was inserted last week to illustrate the sad event. Co.-Quartermaster-Sergeant James Hampson, writing to Mrs. Rose, says :—" I am fxtremely sorry to have to say that Private Rose was killed in action on September 27th. .. . . His comrades are very sorry to have lost him, and I sincerely hope that the fact that he was a most willing worker and good -oldier will help you to feel that comfort and consolation which such knowledge is calculated</p>
