        <p>PRIVATE T. RIC HARDSON. Killed.</p>
        <p>a comrade, Private, Jack Fisher, of 83, Pier- point-street, who stated, "I know for sure that a Warrington fellow was killed by the same shell as my old 'pal.' His name was Tom Richarason. I don't know where he lived, but he used to mention about Sankey Bridges." Private Richardson, who was 29 years of age, worked for Messrs. Rylands Ltd. for fourteen years, and then took up the duties of a special policeman to guard Winwick Waterworks. Re joined the South Lancs. Regiment ' twelve months last May.. As a boy he attended Silver- street School, and in later years he was one of the congregation at the Spiritualist Room, Sankey-street.</p>
        <p>SGNLR. G. H. HAZLEHURST Meets With' Fatal Burning Accident in France. An accident at the Front has resulted in the death by burning of Signaller George Henry Hazlehurst, of the County Palatine Artillery,</p>
