        <p>RIFLEMAN E. APPLETON Wounded.</p>
        <p>and N.-W. Railway prior to enlisting in Decem- ber of 1914. He went to the Front in May of the following year, and has figured in many of the biggest engagements. • • • , PRIVATE J. HANSON. Crosfield's Man Wounded Soon Alter Transfer. Private Joseph_ Hanson, a married man with a little girl, who live at 58, Winwick-road, has ;)een wounded in the hand during a charge in the present fighting in the neighbourhood. of the Somme He enlisted in the Territorials two years ago, but was transferred to the York and Lancaster Regiment, to which regiment he was drafted out .three weeks before. he received his injury. At the time he 'enlisted the, was engaged in Crosfield's box room. • j Private Hanson, whose father is Mr. Joseph</p>
