        <p>PRIVATE W. PYE. Wounded. Hamilton-street School, 'and formerly worked for Messrs. E. Richardson and Sons, Ltd., Bridge-street. Tx7enty-six years of age, Private Pye attended Cairo-street Chapel and Sunday School, and his brother, Sapper Joseph Pye; is serving with the Royal Engineers. PRIVATE WILLIAM ANDREWS. One Of The Regulars Suffering From Septic Poisoning. Mrs. L. Andrews, 22, Algernon-street, wife of Private William Andrews, South Lanca- shire 'Regiment, has been informed that her husband is ifi hospital with septic poisoning in the right knee. Ile is now in Queen Mary's Hospital, Whalley. This is the second time he has been laid up, having been wounded at Hooge on June 16th of last year. Altogether,. Private Andrews has been with the colours twelve years, being in the latter part, of the Boer War, and, subsequently; spending seven years in India. Brought up and educated.. at the Padgate</p>
