</p>
        <p>PRIVATE W. ANDREWS. Wounded.</p>
        <p>Cottage Homes, Private Andrews was in .the employ of Messrs. Joseph Crosfield and Sons. Ltd., when, realising his country's peril, he rejoined the Army. He is thirty years of age, and when, at home attends St. Clement's Mis- sion Church. PRIVATE T. ADAMS. Five Comrades Injured By One Shell. Private -Thomas Adams, South Lanes: Regi- ment, has been wounded in the left knee and right ankle by shrapnel. At present he lies in a West Lothian hospital. Writing home, he saws that Private Bracegirdle and Private Denton' have recently died of wounds, five com- rades.being wounded by the one shell.. Private Adams is a - son Of Mrs.</p>
        <p>a shrapnel wound in his head. A hospital card to his mother at Booth's Hill said he had been admitted into hospital at Oxford. In a later letter the gallant soldier states that the shrapnel has not yet been lemoved. Private Jack Shaw answered his group call and was drafted to France about three mouths ago. He is 40 years of age, was educated at Lymm School and worshipped at the Parish Church. Prior to enlisting he was employed as a salt worker by Messrs. Charles Moore, and Co., of Heatley. His brother, ex-Private Richard Shaw, also of the Cheshire Regiment, was recently discharged after about 18 months in France. PRIVATE HERBERT BUCKLEY DIES OF WOUNDS. Private Herbert Buckley has died of wounds. As we only received the information as we were going to press we are unable to give any particulars. The late soldier was a married man and leaves a wife and four 'children, who reside at Rush Green. CHESHIRE VOLUNTEER REGIMENT Lynnn Platoon : No. 1 Battalion. B COMPANY. Tuesday, October 31st.-7.20 p.m., Recruits' Drill; 8 p.m., Platoon Drill. Thursday, November 2nd.-7.30 p.m., Recruits' Drill; 8 p.m., Platoon Drill. Orderlies for week.—Sergeant Wood, Privates Parker and Gould. By Order, G. R. WILLIAMSON, Lieut.</p>
